Z||000003||fiero56||10-08-1999||08:33 AM||||I Would have to say that your heater core is leaking.  I have also heard that overhead gauges,(oil, volt, etc) like to steam up also.  Many people on the "other list" have spoken of these symotoms before, and it was, I believe, always the heater core.  Shouldn't be too hard to replace (they said), but then again, it isn't the most fun Fiero repair to do.  I have never had one go, or have to replace one, so I am just going on what I've heard.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 10-08-1999).]||||reg||11
